SWEET HFS: answer protection-class queries only for proven unprotected files

The iOS Foundation mmap-if-safe path requires F_GETPROTECTIONCLASS. Preserve
unsupported protected operations while reporting the native no-entry class only
for regular files on a non-protected, non-CoreStorage, consistent mount with no
volume or file cprotect attribute key. Inspect B-tree keys directly so malformed
protection records or orphaned extents cannot become false absence.

diff --git a/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_vnops.c b/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_vnops.c
--- a/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_vnops.c
